    {
      "role": "MAIN",
      "node": {
        "id": 137855,
        "name": {
          "full": "Yi Huan",
          "native": "桓騎",
          "alternative": [
            "The Beheader",
            "Kan Ki"
          ]
        },
        "image": {
          "large": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b137855-2DbejZ4TErnw.png"
        },
        "description": "Yi Huan is a Vice General who serves in Great General Ao Meng's army. In the past, he was a bandit leader with the moniker Yi Huan the Beheader.\n\nHis personality is said to be extremely brutal as he has no qualms in killing surrendered soldiers and personally beheaded every person in any city or village he conquered. This is shown in how he sends Wei soldiers, who have been severely tortured, along with bags of eyeballs back to their camp to decrease morale and incite fear.\n\nHe always has an arrogant smirk on his face and talks in a crude manner at times. He shows no respect for his foes as he calls Feng Xuan \"an old fart\" and \"trash\" before killing him. He is exhibits a sense of humor and sarcasm as in the case when a fellow crew member asked him why he made an unskilled man named Ogiko as 1000-man commander of The Yi Huan army, he replied \"Gyahaha cause it's funny obviously.\"\n\nHe also has a cool demeanor and almost never displays any shock no matter how bad the situation is. Yi Huan also shows a very dark side as he toys with Xi Bai Gui by dangling the idea of escape from death if he begged for his life then stabbed him several times after he refused to grovel.\n\nHe does exhibits a sense of loyalty exclusive to Ao Meng by holding the rank of Vice General in his army and coming when summoned as demonstrated when Tang Zhang used Ao Meng's name, as he knew that Yi Huan would simply ignore an request for a conversation with him.",
        "gender": null,
        "age": null
      },
      "voiceActors": [
